# Coeus working/intermediate data — regenerated fresh by build scripts each
# run. No page on the live site reads these directly (they exist purely to
# feed Coeus's generation step), so there's no reason to version them.
data/dfs/
dfs/
evidence/
evidence_bootstrap/

# Coeus's actual prompt engineering (Master Prompt, DFS/Prop Standards) —
# kept private for now, per decision on 2026-08-12. This is real strategic
# work; anyone with the raw prompt text could copy it wholesale into their
# own tool. Revisit if/when there's a reason to make it public.
prompts/

# Debug/audit siblings of generated DFS reports — full prompt+evidence
# dumps used for reviewing a report before publishing, not meant for public
# consumption. The .md reports themselves ARE tracked (not excluded here) —
# only these two file types are kept out.
dfs_breakdowns/**/*_prompt.json
dfs_breakdowns/**/*_prompt_full.txt

# Game Breakdowns — made public on 2026-08-15 after review and approval
# (one report explicitly designated the quality reference / "gold
# standard"). Same treatment as dfs_breakdowns above: the .md reports
# themselves ARE tracked; only the debug/audit siblings (full prompt+
# evidence dumps, not meant for public consumption) are kept out.
game_breakdowns/**/*_prompt.json
game_breakdowns/**/*_prompt_full.txt

# dfs_weekly/ — brand new report type (Aug 21 2026), kept fully private
# for now, including the .md reports themselves — same principle as
# Game Breakdowns and DFS reports before it: private until reviewed and
# approved, not just until it runs without crashing. Three real bugs
# were found and fixed in the same session this was built (the lineup
# validator's TE-count logic, the Stacks section's definition of a real
# stack, and a role-security rule for the Lineup of the Week) — review
# is explicitly not finished yet. Once it is, narrow this to just the
# *_prompt.json/*_prompt_full.txt debug siblings, matching the pattern
# already used for game_breakdowns/dfs_breakdowns above.
dfs_weekly/
